            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>For mountain people, Dolly Parton was never simply a celebrity. She was proof.</p><p><br></p><p>Proof that leaving Appalachia did not require disowning it. That ambition and generosity could live in the same rhinestone-covered body. That a woman could be funny without becoming a joke, poor without being pitied, and Southern without making herself smaller.</p><p><br></p><p>When Parton died on August 25, 2026, she left behind songs, businesses, books, and an enormous cultural absence. </p><p>“There will never ever be another you,” fellow country legend Reba McEntire wrote on Instagram. </p><p><br></p><p>This simple statement couldn’t be truer. The question is not who replaces Dolly but instead, who carries forward all the amazing things she built.</p></div>
